<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- W3C SCXML 6.4.3: an `<invoke>` names its child through an expression,
     and the expression cannot be evaluated. The clause places the
     obligation on the Processor rather than on the author: evaluation
     happens at invoke-fire time, and a failure raises `error.execution`.
     No child starts.

     This is a separate obligation from "the evaluated string selects the
     child", which the AOT backends do not implement and which
     docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.13 states as a residue. That residue is
     why this fixture exists in this shape: the child every stub backend
     spawns is an immediate `<final>`, so `done.invoke` arrives on a
     successful evaluation whatever the value was. A fixture built on the
     value would therefore measure nothing on five of six backends. A
     fixture built on the FAILURE measures the one thing the clause makes
     every channel answer for.

     Measured 2026-09-20, before this fixture existed: four AOT backends
     evaluated the expression and raised, Kotlin evaluated it and raised,
     and Python did not evaluate it at all — so a document whose expression
     could not be evaluated started its child there as though nothing were
     wrong. Nothing in the tree could see the difference, because every
     other invoke fixture uses an expression that evaluates.

       raises error.execution     reaches `pass`
       evaluates nothing          `done.invoke` arrives, reaches `fail`

     `target` is DECLARED and holds null on purpose. An undeclared bare
     identifier is refused at build time (§3.6), so a fixture reaching for
     one would be a rejection rather than a runtime failure, and would
     never reach the clause this is about. Indexing a null value is a
     runtime error in every expression runtime SCE lowers to.

     Single-axis: no `<param>`, no `<finalize>`, no second `<invoke>`, and
     the `type` is the one SCXML processor URI shorthand so nothing here
     can be mistaken for §6.4.1 unsupported-type classification.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" initial="probe"
       name="invoke_expression_failure_is_reported">
    <datamodel>
        <data id="target" expr="null"/>
    </datamodel>
    <state id="probe">
        <invoke type="scxml" srcexpr="target.path"/>
        <transition event="error.execution" target="pass"/>
        <transition event="done.invoke" target="fail"/>
    </state>
    <final id="pass"/>
    <final id="fail"/>
</scxml>
